      "description": "Make any sound strummable.\n\nHold SAMPLE and make a sound: your voice, a wine glass, a car horn, your cat. GLIMR turns it into an instrument you play like a harp. Pick a chord, sweep your finger across the strings, and your sound rings out in tune and in harmony.\n\nSAMPLE ANYTHING\n- Hold to sample from the mic. GLIMR waits for your sound, so there's no dead air at the start.\n- GLIMR finds the pitch for you, or you can set the root yourself.\n- Trim, fade, reverse and normalize your samples, or import your own audio files.\n\nPLAY CHORDS WITH ONE FINGER\n- Eight chord types in every key: major, minor, 7th, major 7th, minor 7th, diminished, augmented and sus4.\n- Strum the strings, or tap them one at a time. Strum faster to play louder.\n- Shape the sound with LOFI, DRIVE and CHORUS, plus delay and reverb. The delay locks to your tempo.\n\nBUILT-IN RHYTHM BOX\n- Eight grooves: rock, pop, disco, samba, waltz, bossa, lo-fi and ballad.\n- Edit any pattern: tap to add a hit, drag up or down to set how hard it hits.\n- Set the tempo with tap tempo, or type it in.\n\nRECORD AND TAKE IT ANYWHERE\n- Tap REC to capture what you play.\n- Share the strings and drums as separate 24-bit WAV files, ready to mix.\n- Export your strings as MIDI and rebuild the part in your DAW.\n- Send takes to Files, AirDrop or any app.\n\nPLAY YOUR DAW FROM THE STRINGS\n- Turn on MIDI out in Settings and GLIMR becomes a MIDI controller.\n- Strums, chords and drums play any synth or DAW over USB or Wi-Fi.\n\nWorks on iPhone and iPad. No account, no subscription, no ads. Your sounds stay on your device.",
